This was my second ascension in the 2005 Tournament. This was a
Chaotic orcish barbarian - I wouldn't normally choose an orc, but I
was still entertaining the idea that I might ascend one character of
each race.

The game started fairly normally - couple of shops in the first few
levels, the minetown altar coaligned (always nice), another altar on
DL 8; then I found a Wizard's bones on the Oracle level, DL 9 - thanks
for the CoMR, sness! That CoMR would prove very valuable.

I slugged down the main dungeon robbing some more shops, but then
found Ludious on DL 11 - as shallow as it can be. I retreated
initially from a fire elemental, but returned as soon as I had the
appropriate resistance. Naturally this netted me AC 0, and the one
real find; Grayswandir in the heap of soldier corpses. Sure, it
blasted me every time I wielded it, but I had plenty of hitpoints.

Shortly afterwards I was crowned, which appears to have netted me
Stormbringer, which I kept as a backup weapon. Against certain
opponents the level-draining is very useful.

Same-race sacrifice let me dump Jubilex and Yeenoghu in unused
branches; I think this may have been done at the coaligned temple on
14, where I also moved my stash.

Medusa on 24; Castle on 26; I held back a PoGL and unholy water in
case I didn't find a cPoGL, genocided L, and assembled a shopping list
at the Castle. Unfortunately the wand was 0:2 and I had had little
luck with finding what I needed; I kept the bones CoMR, a SoR which I
think came from Perseus, used a black dragon scale mail I'd made (I
know it doesn't work through reflection anyway, but that was just what
I happened to have, and wished up a bag of holding, boots of speed, a
helm of telepathy, gauntlets of power, and a magic marker. Normally I
like GDSM and displacement, but with this shortage of wishes there was
nothing to be done.

I cleared Gehennom using the technique of teleporting to the bottom
with a demon lord - at this point it struck me that donating the spare
Ludious gold for a big whack of clairvoyance would have been a useful
thing to do to speed up looking for Vlad's stairs. Next game I'll
remember.  I did see Dispater and Geryon, but fortunately no
Demogorgon - the only named demon I didn't encounter.

I dropped care packages on DL 14 and DL 1, alchemised up 36 bPoFH, and
went off and killed Rodney. A stylish entrance via telecontrol to the
Sanctum put me down not five moves from the inner sanctum's door (I
had a WoSDD, of course) and a stylish exit via cPoGL got me out in
almost no time at all. As a result of this and the general Chaotic
ease in Gehennom, I didn't get malignant-auraed until I was checking
the stash on DL 14. I also got teleport control from a Rodney corpse,
which let me free up a ring slot.

I don't seem to have many records of the Endgame, which suggests to me
it was fairly routine. These days I don't seem to have much difficulty
evading trouble on Air; getting some source of levitation which does
not preclude being Very Fast is important, and the Heart of Ahriman
does perfectly well for that. From the final map and the kill list it
must have been third altar, which is always a pain.

